The sample Batch files illustrate a way to turn off your mouse menu
before running an editor or file directory program from telix.  If 
the programs that you run from telix have their own mouse support, 
they will shut off TLXZMENU.  Construct a batch file to call your 
program and disable TLXZMENU.  In your batch file, after the program 
name, enter the commands to re-install TLXZMENU.  In telix put your 
batch file's name in place of the program's name.
